IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcpp-prohibited-practices`

-- Human Cloning and Other Prohibited Practices Act 2004, ss 2, 5 to 13, 14(3), (4), (6), 16, 17 and 18 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_human-cloning-and-other-prohibited-practices-act-2004.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`an IVF embryo on day 5 in the laboratory` MEANS Embryo WITH
    `is live` IS TRUE
    `has a human or altered human genome` IS TRUE
    `is an animal embryo` IS FALSE
    `days of development, excluding suspension` IS 5
    `days developing outside the body of a woman, excluding suspension` IS 5
    `created by fertilisation of a human egg by human sperm (not embryo splitting)` IS TRUE
    `is a genetic copy of another living or dead human` IS FALSE
    `was removed from a woman by a person intending to collect a viable embryo` IS FALSE
    `is prescribed to be a prohibited embryo` IS FALSE

